Thread.Sleep(2000);
Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
```

**Problem:** A hard 2-second sleep makes the test slow and non-deterministic. On a slow CI agent, 2 s may not be enough; on a fast machine, it wastes time.

**Fix:** Use async/await with a polling mechanism or a synchronization primitive:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    await processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);

    Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures and a slower test suite (Camara et al., SAST 2021 links Sleepy Test to flakiness).

