### 🟡 MEDIUM SEVERITY

#### 5. Eager Test
**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 57)

```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);

Assert.AreEqual("Completed", order.Status);
```

**Problem:** 7 distinct production methods are called. When this test fails, you can't tell which step broke without debugging. This is a unit test class, not an integration suite.

**Fix:** Test each step independently, or if a workflow test is needed, mark it as integration:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow failure diagnosis; any of 7 methods breaking produces the same unhelpful "Status ≠ Completed" message.

